{"id": "EUVD-2026-104480", "enisaUuid": "997c38df-955d-36f1-a92b-32734f7ad73b", "description": "AIOHTTP is an asynchronous HTTP client/server framework for asyncio and Python. Prior to 3.14.4, keepalive timeout handling is absent during the initial portion of a request. An attacker can keep an idle connection open indefinitely before sending any request data, consuming server connection capacity. This issue is fixed in version 3.14.4.", "datePublished": "2026-10-19T16:47:35", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T16:47:35", "baseScore": 8.2, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:P/PR:N/UI:N/VC:N/VI:N/VA:H/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://github.com/aio-libs/aiohttp/security/advisories/GHSA-5wr8-gcqf-gqf3", "https://github.com/aio-libs/aiohttp/commit/be846822b4b3a5a54b6163e794b42dc06fba54a3", "https://github.com/aio-libs/aiohttp/releases/tag/v3.14.4"], "aliases": ["GHSA-5wr8-gcqf-gqf3", "CVE-2026-111064"], "assigner": "GitHub_M", "epss": 0.4, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "69afc5ee-24f5-3cd7-ad9a-7c0a7a0219be", "product": {"name": "aiohttp", "vendor": {"name": "aio-libs"}}, "product_version": "< 3.14.4"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "a436e39a-7eae-3582-a1b2-75033c0dd6e2", "vendor": {"name": "aio-libs"}}], "isExploited": false}